    "avg_execution_time_ms": null,
    "story": "# Basic F2L Insertion - The Foundation\n\nThis is the most fundamental F2L algorithm in CFOP - a simple setup move followed by the sexy move (R U' R'). Mastering this will build the foundation for all your F2L techniques.\n\n## Execution Tips\n\n**The Setup Move (U):**\n- Use your left index finger for the U turn\n- Keep your right hand ready in home position (thumb on D, index on F, middle on R)\n\n**The Sexy Move (R U' R'):**\n- R: Push with right index finger\n- U': Flick with left index (double turn feels smoother than two singles)\n- R': Pull back with right index\n\n**Smooth Flow:**\nThe entire sequence should feel like one continuous motion: Setup → Push → Flick-Flick → Pull. Practice until you can execute it in under 0.5 seconds.\n\n## When to Use\n\n✅ **Best for:** When the pair is already together and just needs insertion\n✅ **Speed:** Very fast execution (1-1.5 TPS for beginners, 3+ TPS for advanced)\n✅ **Recognition:** Instant - you see the white on top, pieces aligned\n\n## Fingertrick Optimization\n\n**Beginner:** Four separate moves\n**Intermediate:** Combine U' into one smooth double flick\n**Advanced:** Pre-position the U move during your cross, so you start directly with R U' R'\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n❌ Pausing between U and R - keep it flowing\n❌ Using index finger for both U and U' - use index and middle for double flick\n❌ Rotating the cube - this case should NEVER need a rotation\n\n## Practice Drill\n\nExecute this algorithm 50 times in a row, timing yourself:\n- **Goal 1:** Under 1 second each (50 seconds total)\n- **Goal 2:** Under 0.7 seconds each (35 seconds total)  \n- **Goal 3:** Under 0.5 seconds each (25 seconds total)\n\n## Related Algorithms\n\nCompare with [Algorithm 2](deddal://alg/F2L-01-FR/1) which uses F moves instead - same result, different feel.\n\n---\n\n**💡 Pro Tip:** This algorithm is so common that top solvers execute it without thinking. It should become pure muscle memory - practice while watching TV!",
    "created_at": "2025-11-08T19:33:24.526Z"
  },
